From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:07:35 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] mshtml: ~75 element and document event properties,
 document.embeds/plugins/nameProp/URLUnencoded (3016)

The on* properties of IHTMLElement..7 and IHTMLDocument..7 that had no event
table entry returned E_NOTIMPL, which raised a script error for assignments
such as elem.oncut = fn or elem.onbeforeupdate = fn. The events (the copy, cut,
drag and drop family, the media events, select, reset, invalid, the Internet
Explorer data binding and layout events, mouseleave and others) now have rows in
the event table, flagged as not supported, so handlers can be set, read and
cleared like the ones that existed already.

IHTMLDocument2::embeds and plugins return the Gecko collections, nameProp the
title (or the last part of the URL), and IHTMLDocument4::URLUnencoded the
unescaped URL.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XZFS4SPPzeH5d2c1MuzqCS

